-- title:
--   Invertibility of an ideal sheaf is local on an open cover
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme, let $\mathcal{U}$ be an open cover of $X$ (a jointly surjective family of open immersions $\mathcal{U}.f\,i \colon \mathcal{U}.obj\,i \to X$), and let $I$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on $X$. The predicate `IsInvertible` for ideal sheaf data $J$ on a scheme $Y$ asserts: for every point $y \in Y$ there are an affine open $V \subseteq Y$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(Y, V)$ with $y \in Y.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, together with an element $g$ of the ring $\Gamma(Y, Y.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ which is a non-zero-divisor and whose span $(g)$ equals the ideal assigned by $J$ to the affine open $Y.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f$. The hypothesis is that for every index $i$ the pullback $I.\mathrm{comap}\,(\mathcal{U}.f\,i)$ of $I$ along the $i$-th member of the cover satisfies this predicate on $\mathcal{U}.obj\,i$. The conclusion is that $I$ itself satisfies it on $X$.
--
--   This is the gluing direction of the statement that being an effective Cartier divisor (an ideal sheaf locally generated by a single non-zero-divisor) is a local property, the restriction direction being invariance of the predicate under pullback along an open immersion. It is used to verify invertibility of ideal sheaves attached to relative effective Cartier divisors, in particular for divisors cut out by points on curves and on schemes smooth of relative dimension one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_IsInvertible_of_forall_comap_openCover.lean

